,"g":"sights","k":"museum","la":-32.054887,"lo":115.739721,"d":373,"wd":"Q113667482"},{"n":"Round House","g":"sights","k":"archaeological_site","la":-32.056118,"lo":115.741273,"d":382,"w":"https://www.fremantleroundhouse.com.au/","ph":"+61 8 9336 6897","ad":"15 Captains Lane","ds":"The Round House was the first permanent building built in the Swan River Colony. Constructed in late 1830 and opened in 1831, it is the second oldest surviving European building in Western Australia, after the Wiebbe Hayes Stone Fort on West Wallabi Island. It is located at Arthur Head in Fremantle, and recent heritage assessments and appraisals of the precinct of the Round House incorporate Arthur Head.","wpu":"Round House (Western Australia)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Roundhouse_gnangarra-1.jpg/960px-Roundhouse_gnangarra-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Moores Building Art Space","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":-32.056249,"lo":115.744797,"d":399,"ph":"+61 8 9432 9555"},{"n":"Western Australian Maritime Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":-32.054725,"lo":115.738898,"d":431,"h":"Mo-Su 09:30-17:00","w":"https://www.museum.wa.gov.au/museums/wa-maritime-museum","ph":"+61 8 9437 8444","wp":"en:Western Australian Museum","wd":"Q3567483","ad":"Victoria Quay","wifi":1,"ds":"The Western Australian Museum is a statutory authority within the Culture and the Arts Portfolio, established under the Museum Act 1969. The museum has six main sites. The state museum, WA Museum Boola Bardip, is located in the Perth Cultural Centre.","wpu":"Western Australian Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Boola_bardip_151120_gnangarra-101.jpg/960px-Boola_bardip_151120_gnangarra-101.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"HMAS Ovens","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":-32.055251,"lo":115.738949,"d":456,"wp":"en:HMAS Ovens","wd":"Q9284699","ds":"HMAS Ovens (S 70) is an Oberon-class submarine, formerly of the Royal Australian Navy (RAN). She was one of six Oberons built for the Royal Australian Navy by the Scottish Scotts Shipbuilding & Engineering Company, and entered service in 1969. The vessel was named for Irishman and Australian explorer John Ovens (1788–1825) and for whom the Victorian river Ovens was named.","wpu":"HMAS Ovens","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/HMAS_Ovens%2C_Fremantle.jpg/960px-HMAS_Ovens%2C_Fremantle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Western Australian Museum Shipwrecks","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":-32.057139,"lo":115.742477,"d":462,"w":"https://www.museum.wa.gov.au/explore/education/wa-shipwrecks-museum"},{"n":"Vasco da Gama Memorial","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":-32.057557,"lo":115.743717,"d":511},{"n":"Explorers' Monument","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":-32.057512,"lo":115.744227,"d":514,"ds":"The Maitland Brown Memorial, also known as Explorers' Monument, is a monument located in Esplanade Park in Fremantle, Western Australia.","wpu":"Explorers' Monument (Western Australia)","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/46/Explorers%27_monument_%28bust%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Bathers Beach","g":"sights","k":"beach","la":-32.057809,"lo":115.741234,"d":559,"wp":"en:Bathers Beach, Fremantle","wd":"Q4869003","ds":"Bathers Beach, also known as Whalers Beach, is a section of coastline that has a written history since the European settlement of what is now called Fremantle, Western Australia. In the 1890s it was bounded to the south by the Long and Short jetties. In the 1930s and 1940s it was called City Beach.","wpu":"Bathers Beach, Fremantle","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/AUS_Perth%2C_Fremantle%2C_Bathers_Beach_024.jpg/960px-AUS_Perth%2C_Fremantle%2C_Bathers_Beach_024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"The Esplanade Hotel","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":-32.05742,"lo":115.74633,"d":583,"w":"https://www.rydges.com/accommodation/perth-wa/esplanade-hotel-fremantle-by-rydges/","ph":"+61 8 9432 4000","wp":"en:Esplanade Hotel (Fremantle)","wd":"Q5399021","ad":"46-54 Marine Terrace","wifi":1,"ds":"The Esplanade Hotel is a hotel located opposite Esplanade Park, on the corner of Essex Street and Marine Terrace, Fremantle, Western Australia. The building stands on the site of the first building used for housing convicts transported from Great Britain in 1850.","wpu":"Esplanade Hotel (Fremantle)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Esplanade_Hotel_Fremantle2.jpg/960px-Esplanade_Hotel_Fremantle2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Nyisztor Studio","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":-32.056839,"lo":115.747959,"d":632},{"n":"The Jetty","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":-32.058872,"lo":115.743436,"d":654,"w":"https://www.monumentaustralia.org.au/themes/technology/industry/display/60483-%22to-the-fishermen%22-the-jetty","wd":"Q106864989","ds":"\"The Jetty\" commemorates the local fisherman who started the fishing industry in Fremantle. The memorial incorporates 12 timber columns, the names of 608 fishermen who pioneered the industry in Fremantle, and two bronze sculptures. The names listed are t"},{"n":"Fremantle Prison","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":-32.055079,"lo":115.752707,"d":943,"w":"https://fremantleprison.com.au/","ph":"+61 8 9336 9200","ds":"Fremantle Prison, sometimes referred to as Fremantle Gaol or Fremantle Jail, is a former Australian prison and World Heritage Site in Fremantle, Western Australia. The site includes the prison cellblocks, gatehouse, perimeter walls, cottages, and tunnels. It was initially used for convicts transported from Britain, but was transferred to the colonial government in 1886 for use for locally-sentenced prisoners.","wpu":"Fremantl